Given a closed rectangle R = [a, b] X [c, d], a partition of R of order n consists of two clooections of partition points that break up R into a union of n² subrectangles. 
More specifically, for i, j = 0, ..., n, we introduce the collections {x(sub(i))} and {y(sub(j))}, so that 

		a = x₀ < x₁ < ... < x(sub(x - 1)) x(sub(i)) < ... < x(sub(n)) = b, 

and 	

		c = y₀ < y₁ < ... < y(sub(j - 1)) < y(sub(j)) < ... < y(sub(n)) = d. 

Let Δx(sub(i)) = x(sub(i)) - x(sub(i - 1)) (for i = 1, ..., n) and Δy(sub(j)) = y(sub(j)) - y(sub(j - 1)) (for j = 1, ..., n). 
Note that Δx(sub(i)) and Δy(sub(j)) are just the width and height (respectively) of the ijth subrectangle (reading left to right and bottom to top) of the partition. 
